>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `set_term_ord`

``` hol4
simpLib.set_term_ord : (term * term -> order) -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sets the term order that guards permutative rewrites.

A rewrite is permutative if its two sides are equal up to a permutation
of variables, as with commutativity. With `set_term_ord ord ss`, an
instance `l = r` of an unbounded permutative rewrite is applied only if
`ord (l, r)` is `GREATER`; `ord` should be a total, AC-compatible
order. Bounded rewrites (`Once`, `Ntimes`) are not guarded. A simpset
without this setting uses `Cond_rewr.ac_term_ord`.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>+ SIMP_CONV bool_ss [arithmeticTheory.ADD_COMM] “a + b”;
>> fun reverse_ord p = Cond_rewr.ac_term_ord (swap p);
>> SIMP_CONV (simpLib.set_term_ord reverse_ord bool_ss)
     [arithmeticTheory.ADD_COMM] “a + b”;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.set_cond_depth`](#simpLib.set_cond_depth),
[`BoundedRewrites.Once`](#BoundedRewrites.Once).
